.TH AWCC-MODE 1 "October 2026" "AWCC Linux 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
awcc-mode \- Hardware Performance Profile Actuator and Live Telemetry Governor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B awcc-mode
[\fIPROFILE\fR] [\fIFLAG\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B awcc-mode
actuates acoustic and performance profiles (e.g. \fIbattery\fR, \fIquiet\fR, \fIbalance\fR, \fImid\fR, \fIhigh\fR, \fIultra\fR),
verifies readback fan boost offsets and platform profiles, and seamlessly transitions
into continuous live telemetry monitoring.
.SH PROFILES
.TP
.B battery
Energy saver profile (10/255 boost, ~1,200 RPM acoustic baseline).
.TP
.B quiet
Acoustic silence profile (20/255 boost, ~1,450 RPM acoustic baseline).
.TP
.B balance
Standard dynamic hybrid thermal profile (40/255 boost, ~2,200 RPM).
.TP
.B mid
Moderate gaming thermal profile (75/255 boost, ~3,100 RPM).
.TP
.B high
High-performance thermal profile (120/255 boost, ~3,900 RPM).
.TP
.B ultra
Full acoustic and thermal overboost (255/255 boost, ~4,800\(en5,029 RPM).
.SH FLAGS
.TP
.B \-\-track, \-\-watch, \-w, \-\-monitor, \-m
Actuate the profile and immediately stream continuous live monitoring until Ctrl+C.
.TP
.B \-\-once, \-\-snapshot, \-s, \-\-no\-monitor
Actuate the profile and print a single-shot status matrix without streaming.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet, \-q
Actuate the profile silently without printing telemetry.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR awccctl (1),
.BR awcc-lux-dashboard (1)
